              "path": "drivers/gpu/drm/drm_modes.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 1,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 1,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "/**\n * drm_mode_match_timings_vrr - test modes for timing equality considering VRR\n * @mode1: first mode\n * @mode2: second mode\n *\n * Check to see if the horizontal timings, vertical display, and vertical\n * sync/blanking offsets are equivalent. This is used for Variable Refresh Rate\n * (VRR) where the vtotal can vary, but the relationship between vdisplay,\n * vsync_start, vsync_end, and vtotal remains consistent. Specifically,\n * instead of checking vtotal, vsync_start, and vsync_end directly, it checks\n * the offsets of vsync_start and vsync_end from vtotal.\n *\n * Returns:\n * True if the modes have matching VRR timings, false otherwise.\n */\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "2db167ec25a4b1fabad49f1f278a88b94b55b230",
